<title>SLOVENIA: D&amp;B keeps Slovenian credit rating steady in June.</title>
<headline>D&amp;B keeps Slovenian credit rating steady in June.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit rating agency Dun &amp; Bradstreet said on Thursday it would keep Slovenia's credit rating steady for June following an upbeat OECD report on the country's economic outlook.</p>
<p>The agency awarded Slovenia a DB3a rating, unchanged since June 1996, placing it second in the region behind the Czech Republic and ahead of Poland.</p>
<p>-- Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
</text>
